# Jenga tower, leaning: a second, shorter giant Jenga tower 7.8 m tall and 3 m square, thirteen layers of three pale birch blocks
# (each 3 x 0.6 x 1 m, as in jenga-tower0), every layer turned a quarter turn on the one below and shifted 3.5 cm further towards
# +x, so the whole tower leans over by half a metre. A game near its end: from the fifth to the eleventh layer seven blocks are
# pulled out, side and middle ones, opening slots to see and shoot through, and three of them have fallen and lie at its foot,
# two flat and one on its side, knee-high cover round it.
format 1
collider mesh

# Half the vertices its size would give it: big, simple forms, and dozens of game pieces lie on the board
Detail detail=0.5
    Material material=jenga_wood
        Union
            # Layer 1, blocks along x
            Translate translation=(-0.018, 0.3, -1.000)
                Rotate rotation=(0, -0.0175, 0)
                    RoundBox size=(1.48, 0.298, 0.48) roundness=0.06
            Translate translation=(0.015, 0.3, 0.000)
                Rotate rotation=(0, -0.0214, 0)
                    RoundBox size=(1.48, 0.298, 0.48) roundness=0.06
